2. Deadlock avoidance strategies:
   a. Eliminate Mutual Exclusion: Allow multiple philosophers to use a chopstick simultaneously.
   b. Eliminate Hold and Wait: Implement a signaling mechanism to notify philosophers when a chopstick is available.
   c. Eliminate No Preemption: Introduce a priority system or a time-out mechanism to force philosophers to release chopsticks.
   d. Eliminate Circular Wait: Reorder the philosophers' seats or introduce a central coordinator to manage chopstick allocation.

