To retrieve the username from the JWT token in ASP.NET Core Web API, follow these steps:

1. First, make sure you have installed the necessary packages:

```
dotnet add package Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens
dotnet add package Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer
```

2. In your `Startup.cs`, configure the JWT authentication in the `ConfigureServices` method:

```csharp
public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
{
    // ...

    services.AddAuthentication(options =>
    {
        options.DefaultAuthenticateScheme = CookieAuthenticationDefaults.AuthenticationScheme;
        options.DefaultSignInScheme = CookieAuthenticationDefaults.AuthenticationScheme;
        options.DefaultChallengeScheme = JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme;
    })
    .AddCookie()
    .AddJwtBearer(options =>
    {
        options.TokenValidationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters
        {
            ValidateIssuer = true,
            ValidateAudience = true,
            ValidateLifetime = true,
            ValidateIssuerSigningKey = true,
            ValidIssuer = "your_issuer",
            ValidAudience = "your_audience",
            IssuerSigningKey = new SymmetricSecurityKey(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("your_secret_key"))
        };
    });
}
```

Replace `"your_issuer"` with your issuer, `"your_audience"` with your audience, and `"your_secret_key"` with your secret key.

3. In your controller, you can use the `User` object to retrieve the username from the JWT token:

```csharp
[Authorize]
public IActionResult GetUsername()
{
    var user = User;
    return Ok(user.Identity.Name);
}
```

This will return the username of the authenticated user.

